WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:11.550
75. Whales, Silent Tears. We humans think more and more about the effect of our actions

2
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:17.990
on our environment. We are starting to understand how destroying animal populations can have

3
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:24.750
far-reaching effects on our planet. We're even starting to consider the rights of animals

4
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:31.110
as we think about hunting them. However, we rarely discuss how our actions affect animals'

5
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:39.670
psychological states. Whales are very intelligent and social. They behave in complex, moral

6
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:45.550
ways. They babysit young whales while their mothers look for food. They can be grateful

7
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:52.310
for being rescued. One whale, after being freed from a net, didn't swim away but instead

8
00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:59.950
approached and touched every diver who had helped save her. Whales need company to thrive.

9
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:05.310
They play and interact with many of their species as they travel through the water.

10
00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:12.550
Now, however, there are far fewer animals in many whale species. One French naturalist,

11
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:17.670
Yves Pagalet, believes that whales are getting lonely. He thinks that the effect hunting

12
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:23.510
has on whales affects not only their bodies but their minds as well. The small numbers

13
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:29.590
of whales left behind are confused. They may not understand where the other whales

14
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:37.350
have gone or why. Pagalet warns that lonely, depressed whales could lose their will to

15
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:43.310
live. That means that they don't care about living anymore. They may stop eating or do

16
00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:51.550
other unhealthy things. He thinks that when whales get too lonely, they may stop breeding.

17
00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:58.270
It's not only hunting that lowers whale populations. Nets and other dangerous fishing gear, environmental

18
00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:05.350
pollution, and the use of sonar, using sound waves to navigate, are all creating a new,

19
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:11.150
frightening environment for whales. They may decide that they just don't want to live

20
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:18.950
in it anymore. Then, unfortunately, whales themselves will finish the job that overhunting

21
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.830
started.
